  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence of a sure outcome (or most likely outcome) and prefers the lottery that has such a sure outcome. However, in this case, both lotteries have nearly certain (but not fully certain) zero outcomes, and the reason does not allow differentiation. The individual did not refer to any outcome as sure or certain, nor did they base their decision on avoiding risk or relying on certainty. Instead, their justification was based on maximizing the payoff in the event of a win, given similar low probabilities of winning. There is no alignment between the information considered by the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome) and what the individual actually considered (size of the positive outcome and similarity in winning chances). Therefore, the decision reason was not used by the individual.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
